                <pb facs="1123" n="987" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg987"/>

                <head>No. 696.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Preston to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Hayti</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-06-24"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 24,
                        1888</date>.<lb/>(Received June 25.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>: I have the honor to
                    announce to you that Messrs. C. A. de Chambrun, George S. Boutwell, and James G.
                    Berret are the counsel for the Haytian Government in the case of C. A. Van
                    Bokkelen, which is submitted to Mr. Alexander P. Morse as arbitrator.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stephen Preston.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
